{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/CFA Interpolation Correlation.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/CFA Interpolation Correlation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"cfa interpolation correlation cfa interpolation correlation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/CFA Interpolation Correlation.md","fileName":"CFA Interpolation Correlation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"CFA Interpolation Correlation","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-16 00:47\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Camera Sensor and Synthetic Image Forensics]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Camera Sensor and Synthetic Image Forensics","fakephotos.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/CFA Interpolation Correlation.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/CFA Interpolation Correlation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"cfa interpolation correlation cfa interpolation correlation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/CFA Interpolation Correlation.md","fileName":"CFA Interpolation Correlation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"CFA Interpolation Correlation","heading":"CFA Interpolation Correlation","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"CFA interpolation correlation is the predictable dependence among color values introduced by demosaicing a repeating sensor mosaic. At positions where a channel was not measured, its value is estimated from neighbors, causing the strength and orientation of correlations to vary periodically across the image.\n\nA forensic detector can estimate this pattern locally. A pasted, resampled, or computer-generated region may lack the expected phase or correlation, but different camera algorithms and subsequent compression require the detector to infer the pattern rather than assume one universal rule.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Camera Sensor and Synthetic Image Forensics","fakephoto